{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "aura_lifecycle_and_tuning",
  "spec": ["aura 2", "aura 4.1", "aura 4.2", "aura 5.2", "aura 6.6", "aura 10"],
  "description": "Init creates the nine grids of the 2 table (CLSID by element type, instance, S; work S = 1) in table order, reads the tuning (publishing the base auras), subscribes the five messages in 4.1 order, adds the agent at levels 0, 10, 4, 6 with flags 2 and publishes the registry node; a second Init does nothing; Shutdown removes the node, the agent and the subscriptions, drops every grid and curve; tuning per 10: decays reset to 0.6 / 0.4 before each read, base auras kept when absent, transient arrays reset with short arrays reading 0 [choice], hotspot defaults unless exactly 3 values, a curve property that is a single scalar counts as absent [choice]; no tuning exemplar changes nothing; 0xC53D10AA re-reads only for group 0xE7E2C2DB / instance 0xAA023079; a missing park curve advances state 6 to 7 [choice]. Expected values written by hand from the spec tables.",
